      "abstained": false,
      "answer": "For measles, healthcare personnel should use respiratory protection at least as protective as a fit-tested, NIOSH-certified N95 respirator upon entry into the patient's room or care area, regardless of presumptive evidence of immunity. For SARS, Airborne Precautions include the use of fit-tested NIOSH-approved N95 or higher level respirators, plus eye protection. For measles and varicella-zoster viruses, however, there are no data upon which to base a recommendation for respiratory protection to protect susceptible personnel.",
